meta {
  name: Update Step - Reflection Learning
  type: http
  seq: 15
}

put {
  url: {{baseURL}}/v1/house/:house/young-persons/:youngPersonId/incidents/:id/steps/reflection-learning
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

params:path {
  house: 4
  youngPersonId: 1
  id: 1
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "staff_debrief": "<p>The staff team handled the situation calmly and professionally. John maintained a non-confrontational stance while Sarah offered alternative activities. Communication between staff was clear and effective.</p><p><strong>What worked well:</strong></p><ul><li>De-escalation techniques were appropriately applied</li><li>YP was given space to calm down</li><li>Team worked cohesively</li></ul><p><strong>Emotional impact on staff:</strong> Both staff members felt confident in their response. No additional support needed at this time.</p>",
    "young_person_debrief": "<p>Met with YP 2 hours after incident when calm. YP acknowledged getting frustrated when TV program changed unexpectedly.</p><p><strong>YP's understanding:</strong> Recognizes that throwing remote was wrong and could have hurt someone. Understands that breaking house property has consequences.</p><p><strong>YP's feelings:</strong> Felt angry in the moment but regrets actions now. Worried about being in trouble.</p><p><strong>Plan to avoid repeat:</strong></p><ul><li>YP will use calm corner when feeling frustrated</li><li>Will ask staff for help with feelings before they get too big</li><li>Agreed to apologize to other YPs who were watching TV</li></ul>",
    "manager_review_learning_points": "<p><strong>Manager's Analysis:</strong></p><p>This incident reflects a pattern we've observed over the past 3 weeks where [YP Name] struggles with unexpected changes to routine, particularly around shared activities.</p><p><strong>Key Learning Points:</strong></p><ol><li>Need for better visual scheduling in common areas</li><li>Staff require additional training on recognizing early warning signs specific to this YP</li><li>Current behavior support plan needs updating to address frustration tolerance</li></ol><p><strong>Systemic Improvements:</strong></p><ul><li>Implement TV schedule board in common room</li><li>Update all YP behavior plans by end of month</li><li>Schedule additional de-escalation training for new staff</li><li>Review supervision levels during high-activity periods</li></ul><p><strong>Follow-up Actions:</strong> Scheduled team meeting for [date] to review updated protocols. Will monitor YP's progress over next 2 weeks.</p>"
  }
}

docs {
  # Update Step: Reflection & Learning
  
  This endpoint updates the three reflection/debrief fields for the incident.
  
  ## Fields:
  
  ### 1. `staff_debrief` (richtext, optional)
  **Staff Debrief** - Reflection with involved staff covering:
  - Emotional impact on staff
  - What intervention strategies worked well
  - Learning points from the incident
  - Support needs for staff members
  
  ### 2. `young_person_debrief` (richtext, optional)
  **Young Person Debrief** - Discussion with the child after the incident:
  - YP's understanding of what happened
  - How they were feeling during and after
  - What they learned from the situation
  - Their plan to avoid similar situations
  - Any support they feel they need
  
  ### 3. `manager_review_learning_points` (richtext, optional)
  **Manager Review / Learning Points** - Manager's analysis:
  - Overall assessment and patterns noticed
  - Lessons learned for the team/organization
  - Systemic improvements needed
  - Follow-up actions and timelines
  - Policy or procedure updates required
  
  ## Legacy Fields (Backward Compatibility):
  - `reflection_learning` - General reflection text
  - `preventive_measures` - Preventive measures text
  
  ## Purpose:
  This section enables:
  - Multi-level reflection (staff, YP, management)
  - Continuous improvement
  - Pattern identification
  - Staff and YP development
  - Risk assessment updates
  - Policy improvements
  
  ## Response:
  Returns the updated incident record with all reflection fields.
}
